---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import FinancialStatementKey from "../../components/FinancialStatementKey.astro";
import Glossary from "../../components/Glossary.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import HistoryTimeline from "../../components/HistoryTimeline.astro";
import history from "../../data/history.json";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/usgaap/asc718.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope & Applicability" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Fair Value Measurement – Equity-Classified Awards" },
        { id: "s4", label: "Vesting Conditions – Service and Performance" },
        { id: "s5", label: "Modifications – a Change in Terms" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Cash-Settled vs Equity-Settled – the Classification Divide" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Worked Example – Stock Option Fair Value" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Worked Example – Modification of an Equity Award" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Critical Judgments & Estimates" },
        { id: "s11", label: "ASC 718 vs IFRS 2 – Comprehensive Comparison" },
         { id: "s12", label: "Statement Mapping" },
         { id: "s13", label: "Related Topics" },
       ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">

    <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci"><div class="ctitle ci">Compensation paid in equity instruments</div><div style="font-size: var(--text-small); color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: 1.6;">ASC 718 addresses a distinctive form of compensation: payment not in cash, but in the employer's own equity instruments (stock options, restricted stock, performance shares) or equity-classified derivatives. This creates a compensation cost measured at the fair value of the equity instruments granted, recognised over the vesting period as employees provide service.</div></div>
      <div class="card cs"><div class="ctitle cs">Converged with IFRS 2, with classification differences preserved</div><div style="font-size: var(--text-small); color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: 1.6;">ASC 718 and IFRS 2 both require share-based payment transactions to be recognised as compensation expense based on the fair value of the equity instruments granted, representing a significant achievement of the early FASB/IASB convergence project. However, classification differences for cash-settled awards and modifications remain between the two frameworks.</div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope & Applicability</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">All share-based payment transactions</div><div style="font-size: var(--text-small); color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: 1.6;">ASC 718 applies to ALL share-based payment transactions, including equity-classified awards (stock options, restricted stock, performance shares) and liability-classified awards (cash-settled share-based payments, share appreciation rights). It covers transactions with employees, non-employees, and customers where the payment is in equity instruments.</div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Fair Value Measurement – Equity-Classified Awards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Measurement at grant date</div><div style="font-size: var(--text-small); color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: 1.6;">Equity-classified awards are measured at FAIR VALUE on the GRANT DATE – the date when the employer and employee agree on the terms of the award and the employee begins providing service in exchange for the award. The fair value is typically determined using an option-pricing model such as Black-Scholes or a binomial model, incorporating assumptions about volatility, expected term, risk-free rate, and expected dividends.</div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Vesting Conditions – Service and Performance</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">When compensation cost is recognised</div><div style="font-size: var(--text-small); color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: 1.6;">Compensation cost is recognised over the REQUIRED SERVICE PERIOD – the period during which the employee must complete service to earn the award. MARKET conditions (such as a stock price target) affect the fair value at grant but do NOT accelerate or change the service period. PERFORMANCE conditions (such as revenue targets) affect whether the award vests and require estimation of the probability of achieving the target.</div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Modifications – a Change in Terms</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">When award terms are changed after grant</div><div style="font-size: var(--text-small); color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: 1.6;">If an employer MODIFIES the terms of an equity-classified award after the grant date – such as by lowering the exercise price, extending the exercise period, or changing a performance condition – the incremental fair value of the modification is recognised as ADDITIONAL compensation cost over the remaining required service period. This prevents employers from avoiding recognition by repricing underwater options.</div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Cash-Settled vs Equity-Settled – the Classification Divide</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">A fundamental accounting difference</div><div style="font-size: var(--text-small); color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: 1.6;">EQUITY-SETTLED awards (stock options, restricted stock) are measured at grant-date fair value and recognised over the service period – the fair value does NOT change after grant. CASH-SETTLED awards (cash-settled stock appreciation rights, phantom stock) are REMEASURED at each reporting date to fair value, with changes recognised in period-by-period profit or loss. This remeasurement requirement makes cash-settled awards significantly more volatile in reported compensation cost.</div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Worked Example – Stock Option Fair Value</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Measuring an option-based award</div>
      <div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Grant-date fair value of stock options</div><div class="wk-body">An entity grants 10,000 stock options with an exercise price of $50. Current stock price is $50, risk-free rate is 3%, volatility is 30%, expected term is 5 years, expected dividend yield is 1%. Using Black-Scholes, the grant-date fair value per option is $14.25.</div><div class="wk-answer">Total grant-date fair value = 10,000 options × $14.25 = <strong>$142,500</strong>. If the options vest over a 4-year service period, the entity recognises <strong>$35,625</strong> of compensation expense per year ($142,500 ÷ 4), regardless of the option's eventual exercise price or stock price movement.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Worked Example – Modification of an Equity Award</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Incremental fair value from a repricing</div>
      <div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Modifying underwater options</div><div class="wk-body">After a stock decline, outstanding options with an exercise price of $50 have a current stock price of $35. The employer reduces the exercise price to $30 to retain employees. At modification, the original option fair value was $10 and the revised fair value is $18.</div><div class="wk-answer">Incremental fair value of the modification = $18 − $10 = <strong>$8 per option</strong>. This $8 per-option incremental cost is recognised as ADDITIONAL compensation expense over the remaining vesting period, on top of the original grant-date cost already recognised.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASC 718 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Weighted-average assumptions used in fair value measurement (volatility, expected term, risk-free rate, dividends)</span><span>Total compensation cost recognised and the effect on earnings per share</span><span>Number and weighted-average exercise price of options outstanding, exercisable, and expired</span><span>Cash received from option exercises and tax benefits realised</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Critical Judgments & Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
      <div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Selection of option-pricing model and input assumptions</span><span>Classification as equity-settled vs cash-settled</span><span>Determination of the grant date for complex award structures</span></div></div>
      <div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Expected volatility and expected term of options</span><span>Probability of achieving performance conditions</span><span>Fair value of incremental modification benefits</span></div></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>ASC 718 vs IFRS 2 – Comprehensive Comparison</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison – ASC 718 vs IFRS 2</div>
      <div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">US GAAP (ASC 718)</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IFRS (IFRS 2)</span></div>
      <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Measurement principle</span><span>Grant-date fair value for equity awards</span><span>Grant-date fair value at grant date</span></div>
      <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Cash-settled awards</span><span>Remeasured at each reporting date; changes in P&L</span><span>Same treatment – fair value remeasurement in P&L</span></div>
      <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Market conditions</span><span>Included in grant-date fair value, not affecting service period</span><span>Same treatment</span></div>
      <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Modifications</span><span>Incremental fair value recognised over remaining service</span><span>Similar incremental fair value approach</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="note">ASC 718 and IFRS 2 are among the most closely converged standard pairs in the entire standards landscape, reflecting the early and successful FASB/IASB convergence project on share-based payments.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every ASC 718 event lands</div>
      <div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
      <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Equity award compensation cost</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bp">IS</span></span><span>Recognised over service period; increases equity</span></div>
      <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Cash-settled award remeasurement</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bp">IS</span></span><span>Fair value changes recognised in P&L each period</span></div>
      <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Option exercise</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bc">SCF</span></span><span>Cash received; equity transferred from APIC</span></div>
      </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Related Topics</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
      <div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Topic</span><span>Connection</span></div>
      <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASC 505</span><span>Equity – governs the equity classification and presentation of share-based payments</span></div>
      <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASC 815</span><span>Derivatives and Hedging – determines whether an award contains a derivative requiring separate accounting</span></div>
      <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>IFRS 2</span><span>Share-based Payment – IFRS counterpart, one of the most converged standards</span></div>
      </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <FinancialStatementKey />

  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.ASC718 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>

